WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.180
The release manager creates v1.1.0, adds every available change and asks for review. Changes excluded from releases are not offered.

00:12.180 --> 00:24.180
Every change gets a decision: one is approved as shown, one is reclassified as Security, one is rejected.

00:24.180 --> 00:32.300
With every change decided, the release is approved and one note per audience and language is written.

00:32.300 --> 00:40.120
Publishing freezes the notes; each one can be downloaded.

00:40.120 --> 00:46.880
Anyone can read the published note on the public changelog, without signing in.

00:46.880 --> 00:50.480
The same rule also posts it to the team's Slack channel.
